# Keep ModemManager off the T-Display-K230 console.
#
# The board's CH342K dual USB-UART bridge (1a86:55d2) shows up as two plain
# CDC-ACM ports. /usr/lib/udev/rules.d/80-mm-candidate.rules tags *every* tty
# as a ModemManager candidate with no vendor filtering, so on every
# enumeration ModemManager grabs both ports with TIOCEXCL for ~18 seconds,
# reprograms the UART to its default 57600 while the K230 talks at 115200,
# flashes the line at baud 0, writes "AT" six times and then a binary QCDM
# frame. The result is a burst of mis-framed bytes on our side and junk
# prefixed onto U-Boot's command line on the board's side.
#
# See docs/evidence/ch342-open-garbage.md for the full trace.
#
# Install:
#   sudo install -m0644 tools/99-tdisplay-k230-no-modemmanager.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload
#   # then unplug and replug the console cable
#
# ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE is honoured under every ModemManager filter policy,
# including strict. Tag the usb_device, not the tty, so both ports are
# covered at once.

# Must match SUBSYSTEM=="tty", not "usb". ModemManager tags the tty node
# itself (/usr/lib/udev/rules.d/80-mm-candidate.rules:21 is
# SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ENV{ID_MM_CANDIDATE}="1"), and an ENV{} set on the
# parent usb device does NOT propagate to its tty children. Tagging the
# usb_device left ID_MM_CANDIDATE=1 on ttyACM0 and MM kept probing.
# ATTRS{} walks up the parent chain, so the VID/PID still matches here.
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55d2", ENV{ID_MM_DEVICE_IGNORE}="1"
